Body:
Thanks for this fix. I hit the same bug and want to share a precise repro + a gap this PR doesn't cover.

**Repro (no malformed URL needed):** opening `/app/` matches the `/:dir` route with `dir="app"`. `atob("app")` does not throw in Chromium — it decodes to bytes `[0x6A, 0x9A]`, and the non-fatal `TextDecoder` turns `0x9A` into U+FFFD. Result: `"j�"` becomes the working directory (persisted into the localStorage draft tab), and every prompt fails with `FileSystem.realPath (.../j�) ENOENT`.

**Gap:** this PR only guards the server (fatal decoder + cwd fallbacks). The client-side `decodeDirectory()` in `packages/app/src/pages/directory-layout.tsx` still accepts the decoded U+FFFD value and writes it to the draft tab in localStorage — which explains why the error persists after applying this branch (see @chardskarth's comment). Existing polluted drafts survive a server-side fix.

**Suggested one-line client-side complement:**

```ts
export function decodeDirectory(dir: string): ProjectDirString | undefined {
  const decoded = decode64(dir)
  if (!decoded) return
  if (base64Encode(decoded) !== dir) return // round-trip check, same pattern as requireServerKey()
  return ProjectDirString.make(decoded)
}
```

Verified on 1.18.16 and 1.17.20 (Windows, web UI). Happy to open a separate PR for the app-layer part if useful.

**Extending this request: monthly window + last top-up anchor**

#41981 (closed as dup of this) asked for balance + monthly usage/limit + reset timestamps on the usage API. Folding that scope in here:

The existing `GET /zen/go/v1/usage` (#16513) returns plan-window percentages only — no monetary amounts. For Zen balance-billing workspaces, quota tools (opencode-quota, etc.) still scrape the billing page HTML. Proposal: sibling endpoint `GET /zen/v1/workspace/usage` returning:

```json
{
  "generatedAt": "...",
  "currency": "USD",
  "balance": {
    "amount": 12.34,
    "updatedAt": "...",
    "percentOfLastTopUp": 61.7,
    "lastTopUp": { "amount": 20.00, "at": "..." }
  },
  "usage": {
    "monthly": {
      "status": "ok",
      "used": 42.10,
      "limit": 100.00,
      "remaining": 57.90,
      "percent": 42.1,
      "resetsAt": "..."
    }
  }
}
```

Key points:
- `percentOfLastTopUp` = `balance / lastTopUp.amount * 100` — "of what I last paid, X% remains"; server-computed, `null` when no anchor
- Monthly window mirrors the go endpoint's shape but with absolute USD values (server owns the math, kills the 100M-units conversion clients hardcode)
- `status` server-derived: ok / near_limit / rate_limited / blocked
